WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.868
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.367
We're hanging out with
Eddie Redmayne.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.100
Now, Eddie, you play
Newt Scamander

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.968
in the
"Fantastic Beasts" movies.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.801
So we thought we'd put
your knowledge of the character

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:13.000
to the test in a game called
"Know Your Role."

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.067
Here we go. Okay, here we go.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.534
-♪ Know your role ♪

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:20.834
-Now, here's how it works.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:24.167
I'm going to give you an obscure
fact about your character

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:27.067
or the wizarding world --
universe in general.

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.300
And you have to tell me
if you think

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.200
that statement is true or false.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.901
It might get a little tricky,

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:35.000
'cause your character has
a pretty wild backstory.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.701
Are you ready for this?
-I am. Go for it.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:37.801
-Okay.
-Hit me.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.634
-American wiz--
And you guys can help.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:42.033
Or maybe not.
Up to you, up to you.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:45.300
American wizards use --
American wizards use currency

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.033
known as dragots and sprinks.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.033
[ Audience shouting "False!" ]

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:52.133
-Oh, guys, you are so helpful.

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.934
Thank you. False.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:57.000
-That is true, actually.
[ Buzzer ]

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.667
I sold that.
I sold sprinks funny on purpose.

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:02.100
-But it was such confidence
from the audience.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.300
-I know, I know.
I was like, "Sprinks."

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.300
Yeah, I hit that,
but that was --

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.901
Yeah, that actually is true.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:09.267
Dragots and sprinks --
American wizards.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.300
There you go.
-Perfect.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.067
-Your character, Newt Scamander,

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:16.968
once had a relationship with
a hippogriff named Buckbeak.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:21.200
-A relationship?
That's all kinds of dodgy.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.234
-Yeah, a relationship.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.634
It could be platonic.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:28.501
-Well, I remember Newt's mom
bred and raised hippogriffs.

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.734
So I'm going to go with true.

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:33.534
-False. We know...
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.133
So far, you're doing great.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.534
-That's, like,
a really cruel audience.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.200
-No, they're doing --
They're playing with us.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.267
It's really good. I love this.
Thank you, guys.

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.367
I love this.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.834
Alright, a new word
was created for

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:47.067
the "Fantastic Beasts" movie,
shriekelnoir,

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.934
which is a magical ability to

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.634
change size to fit
into small spaces.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:53.300
-No, and I love that
I know this,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.534
because there was a word
called choranaptyxic.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.801
-That's correct.
[ Buzzer ]

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.133
That is correct.
That's not a buzzer.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:01.234
That's a correct.
[ Ding ]

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.734
Yeah, that's --
That is exactly right.

00:02:03.734 --> 00:02:04.968
-Thank you.

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.200
-How do you pronounce it?

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.167
-Choranaptyxic. But I love that
you just told me

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:10.400
that it was invented, because
I thought it was a real word.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.534
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
It was invented.

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:12.634
Yeah, just for you.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:13.868
Alright, here we go.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:17.267
Newt was expelled from Hogwarts
for using a spell

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:21.234
that turned his professor's
hands into crab claws.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:25.801
-Newt was expelled from
Hogwarts,

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:31.868
but as far as I'm aware, not for
my sort of "Karate Kid" dance.

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.400
-That is correct. It's false.
Yeah, that is correct.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.534
Yes, you're right.

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:37.400
He was not expelled for
that reason, no.

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:41.567
Newt Scamander's
middle name is Fido.

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:44.267
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:46.267
-Yeah, it is true. Yeah.
[ Ding ]

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:49.100
-Fido Artemis.
-Fido Artemis.

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:52.300
I like that.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.834
Newt is actually able to
temporarily transform himself

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:59.767
into a fantastic beast
known as snardvark.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.234
-I'm desperate for it to be yes.

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:06.701
But -- Can we suggest that for
"Fantastic Beasts 4?"

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.334
-Yeah, yeah. You're correct.

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:11.501
-But the great thing about these
movie is that they're magic.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.367
You can do anything.
-It's all magic. It's all magic.

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:14.834
Alright, this is good.
You're doing great.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.167
You're back. You're back.
-Thanks, man. Back in the room.

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:17.567
-Here we go.

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:23.868
Which of the following beasts is
not featured in Newt's book?

00:03:23.868 --> 00:03:29.868
Glumbumble, nogtail, niffler,

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.834
gugengoggle...

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.133
chizpurfle.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:39.934
-You know, I think
the cameraman is laughing.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.400
-I don't know which one
he's laughing at, but yeah.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.701
-The gugengoggle.
-That is correct.

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:45.167
Gugengoggle is not true.

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:47.167
This guy know his stuff!

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.734
You know your role.
Eddie Redmayne, everybody!

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:53.234
Check out "Fantastic Beasts:
The Secrets of Dumbledore" --

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:54.467
in theaters April 15th.

